  "id": "COMPOUND:15856 - PROTEIN:1919",
  "verbalization": "Phyllaemblicin D appears to exert its biological effects through a series of interconnected targets that ultimately lead to the activation of the Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein. The evidence suggests that Phyllaemblicin D acts as a target for Polyporenic Acid A and Isoscutellarein 8-O-glucoside, both of which are implicated in the regulation of the Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein. This implies that Phyllaemblicin D may influence cellular signaling pathways that are critical for the function of the Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein. Additionally, Phyllaemblicin D is also shown to target WRL68, which is subsequently targeted by 18,19-Dihydroangustine, further reinforcing a chain of interactions that could contribute to the pathophysiology of Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Phyllaemblicin D to modulate key cellular processes involved in the syndrome, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
